{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>ידבר הוא וגם הנה</b> — rashei tevot (initial letters) form the Name of four letters, to tell you that He transmitted to Aaron also the Name and all its epithets." "<b>יצא</b> — two times in the Masorah, defective: יצא לקראתך, יצא המימה. One — the word of Elohim. Two — this one I heard: when HaKadosh Baruch Hu said to Moses 'Go return to Egypt,' the utterance split in two, and was heard by Moses 'Go return' and by Aaron 'Go to meet Moses,' and he went out immediately. Therefore it is defective, to say that he had already gone out. And likewise יצא המימה is defective — he made himself a god and said he does not need his own [bodily functions], and rises early in the morning and goes out to the water for his needs. And this is what was said to him: 'He has already gone out, and behold, he is there.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "The phrase 'אחת דבר אלהים שתים' is rendered literally; Ba'al HaTurim uses it to enumerate the two Masorah occurrences. The antecedent of 'he made himself a god' is Pharaoh, per Exodus 7:15 context; the grammar shifts without explicit subject change."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:54.070794576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}